# Reviewed baseline for scripts/extra-docs.sh (see docs/IRON-LAWS.md).
#
# Each line is MESSAGE<TAB>PATH, matching one distinct ex_doc warning. Every
# entry here is in a GENERATED file that this repository must not hand-edit:
# `mix usage_rules.sync` rewrites AGENTS.md and the usage_rules-built skills on
# every sync. The fix for any of them is upstream, in the package that ships
# the text; when an upstream fix arrives and the entry stops firing, the check
# fails until the entry is deleted here.
#
# Anything in hand-written docs or moduledocs is fixed, never baselined.

# AGENTS.md, from dependency usage-rules.md files (inlined by usage_rules.sync).
# ash_authentication's rules cite AshAuthentication.Info.strategies/1, which its Info
# module does not define (the generated accessor is authentication_strategies/1);
# phoenix's Ecto rules cite validate_number/2, which only exists as /3.
documentation references function "AshAuthentication.Info.strategies/1" but it is undefined or private	AGENTS.md
documentation references function "Ecto.Changeset.validate_number/2" but it is undefined or private	AGENTS.md

# The ash-framework and phoenix-web skills, built by usage_rules.sync from the
# packages' mix task lists. The list includes each installer's hidden `.docs`
# companion module and other @moduledoc false tasks, which ex_doc cannot link.
documentation references module "mix ash_a2ui.install.docs" but it is hidden	.claude/skills/ash-framework/SKILL.md
documentation references module "mix ash_admin.install.docs" but it is hidden	.claude/skills/ash-framework/SKILL.md
